THE CHAIN (LQG spin network → H₂⁺, H₂; each a kernel-checked module)

linkhop — electron hop on one link = 2×2 orthogonal matrix (entries −1/2, √3/2), from bholonomy's hop-amp. Levels ±1.
vertexhop — hop out of a 4-valent vertex along each link. Moving the electron's ½ to the other link-pair has coefficient +1 (6j with a zero entry = Racah's sum); per-link squared amplitudes sum to 1.
nethop — all-½ net: hop to a neighbour sends the link ½→1 two ways, squared amplitudes 1/4 and 3/4, sum 1. Summed: unit-amplitude walk. Hop amplitude t is one number for the whole net.
cover — the hop carries the link's U(1) holonomy, so it moves the link flux by 1. Electron + its flux = one walker on the graph's maximal abelian cover; two walks coincide iff their flux chains agree. Gauss's law after every walk (hexagon, cage). Σn² is a potential on the cover.
fluxsplit — Σn² = Σh² + Σ(n−h)². Σh² = charges' Coulomb part (field-energy = resistance metric). n−h over one coset of integer circulations = charges' class in the graph's abelian group (order = spanning-tree count). Electric term alone: energy between charges = the shorter arc (a string). Foster's theorem: hexagon, cage, complete graph.
sectors — QSD V magnetic loops move no flux between vertices (625 sectors). Vertex energy = function of vertex charge only ⇒ local terms carry no inter-vertex force.
netpiece — diamond net closed at period 2 = the 4-cube graph (16 vertices). Charge energy at separation 1–4: 15/32, 7/12, 61/96, 2/3. Kirchhoff over the rationals.
ringatom, netatom — H = (λ/2)·fluxenergy − t·hop − K·ringloops on the cover; moments at the nucleus = polynomial identities in t, K, λ.
ringbound — ring, exact: (λ/2)R − 2t ≤ E₀ ≤ (λ/2)R, R = eff-resistance = d(N−d)/N (all rings ≤ 8). Lower bound without the dual torus.
cwbound — net, free t, λ: discrete Collatz–Wielandt, min_u (Hψ)_u/ψ_u ≤ E₀ ≤ max_u. Potential/degree extremes checked ⇒ finite bracket on the bond depth.

